WEBVTT

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.360
You got dumped?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.500
Oh, yeah! Big time!

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.340
You're pretty chirpy for
a guy who's just been dumped.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.980
It's better for my health to
talk about it and forget it

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.110
than to keep it inside
and let it brew.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.150
It's not in my nature to let
something like this get me down.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.690
Oh...

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.590
Yeah! I'm gonna drink
and forget her!

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.980
I know it was
partly my fault,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.640
but...but...she didn't have
to dump me like that!

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.320
Sad.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.520
Keiko...

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.680
Keiko!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.100
S-Stop it!

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.300
Keiko! Keiko!

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.710
Stupid Sakamoto!
It's me! It's ME!!

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.260
Summer's here.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.730
Grandma? May I
leave you in charge?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.230
Sure.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.360
I'll be back
by evening.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.910
Go right ahead.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.960
Hey, neighbor?!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.430
I'm so bored.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.850
Thank you for
the ride home.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.710
It's nothing.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.180
There's nothing
like a cold beer

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.390
after sweating it out
playing tennis.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.700
- Wanna join me?
- No thank you.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.700
I'm the third-wheel
anyway. Beer!

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:08.990
Good-bye.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.040
Ms. Otonashi.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:10.830
Yes?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.110
Are you free tomorrow?

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.430
Well, yes.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.400
I'm a club member at
a hotel swimming pool,

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.050
and I'd love to
Invite you as my guest.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:25.550
Pool?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.520
Yes. Tennis is fun,
but in summer

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.680
nothing beats being at the pool
under the shimmering sun.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.290
I'd love to go with you!

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.030
Grandma! I didn't
know you were here!

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.090
Did I interrupt?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.960
I didn't mean that.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.930
I'm so bored every day.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.320
Where's Godai?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.070
Even though I've traveled
so far to see him

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.050
he's been out every day.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.850
He's very busy
with his job hunt.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.980
I see. Of course
you'd be lonely.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.070
It's so nice of you
to understand.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.680
Well then...

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.550
Since Godai can't

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.070
we'd love to take you
to the pool.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.050
How about it
Ms. Otonashi?

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.590
It's decided, then.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.250
I won't get in your way.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.360
I look forward to
seeing you tomorrow!

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.210
I better go buy myself
a bathing suit.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.480
A day at the pool
could be fun.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.180
I'm back!

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.220
Grandma, I'm home.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.230
Don't I look great
in this? Huh?

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.300
Grandma, are you okay?

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.210
What're you doing?

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.300
I bought this to wear at
the hotel pool tomorrow.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:00.980
Hotel pool?

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.230
Coach Mitaka invited me to go.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.670
Mitaka did?

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.980
T-The manager's not
going with you, is she?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:10.920
She is.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:11.980
I knew it!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.660
If you're worried,
you wanna come along, too?

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.730
I-I'm busy looking for a job.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.920
I'm going to take a bath.

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.240
Oh no! It's from last night!

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.170
This is bad...!

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:50.530
Good morning.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.660
Good morning.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.920
Another day of
job-hunting, Godai?

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:57.820
Yes.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.800
It's hard work, isn't it?

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.910
It's going to determine
the rest of my life.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.440
Good luck.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:10.440
I need to be able to tie
my own necktie from now on.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.020
Bye!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.050
Have a good day!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.150
It's going to be
another scorcher.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.020
Here you go.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:55.550
I can't believe I have to
work at a place like this.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:02.880
Here you go.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.670
Manager! This way!

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.920
M-Manager?!

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.310
Thank you so much, Mitaka.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.070
This hotel pool
must be expensive.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.820
Let's not talk about money, okay?

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.090
That's right.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.730
Coach Mitaka is rich.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:29.380
How nice of you
to treat us, too!

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:31.950
I figured this would happen.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.760
He doesn't mind!

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.630
What's another three guests?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.320
Such generosity!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.140
It would have been
so much more fun

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.370
if Godai could
have joined us.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.170
I'm sure it
wouldn't have hurt

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.700
to take a day off
from job-hunting.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.440
Yeah. He's not getting
anywhere anyway.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:51.510
I have my doubts about
whether he'll even graduate.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.120
Even if he graduates, he probably
won't get a job for a while.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.790
Godai's pretty
used to rejection.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.300
He's got a rejection connection.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.790
Those stinkers have some nerve
to talk about me like that!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.260
But what are the odds

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.900
of them coming to the
pool where I work?

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.670
Godai, what're you
mumbling about over here?

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.410
The manager and
the gang are here.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.510
So?

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.380
This is bad.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.450
They think I'm out
looking for a real job.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.550
Why did you lie
to them, Godai?!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.220
Is something
the matter, Ms. Otonashi?

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.740
N-No. It's nothing.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.420
Let's go for a swim.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.550
You shouldn't lie.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.050
I don't care
if you got dumped.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:00.710
Who drank away my rent
for this month?

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:06.220
Don't bring that up.
I got you this job.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.300
That's not all!

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.200
Who do you think
gave me this?

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.170
A hickey?
Where did you get that?

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.430
You put it there!

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:25.670
Me?

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.640
You came onto me
mistaking me for a woman.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.340
No...

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.580
Don't try to deny it.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.020
I'm the one who
feels sick about it!

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.520
Thanks for all the drinks!

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:44.150
This is great!

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.900
Pretend you don't know them.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.050
Here you go.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.300
They're the same
wherever they go.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.450
Damn him!

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:14.450
He's all over the manager,
knowing I'm not around.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.800
I give Godai credit.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.830
I didn't start looking
for work until autumn.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.090
Enjoy.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.470
Please.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.060
Thank you.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.810
What's the matter?

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.790
Nothing.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.050
Please.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:50.420
Yes...

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:56.900
He's treating her
like his girlfriend!

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:03.960
Hey!

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:09.880
It's your turn to
take a lunch break.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:10.990
Okay.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.810
I can't forgive him!

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.610
We're out of beer.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.470
Where's our waiter?

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.980
Someone go buy some.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.850
Having Godai here would
have been convenient.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.490
Hi everybody! You're all here.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:49.480
Yusaku?

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.970
Godai, why are you here?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.490
I'd heard that you were
busy job-hunting.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:59.330
I have some time before
my afternoon interview.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.970
Who knew you had
money for the pool?

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:03.940
I've got pool money!

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.020
Well, come and have a drink!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.370
Go get us another beer.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.270
A pool is no place
for a drink fest.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:13.950
He's right.

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.470
I think I'll go
for another swim.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.410
I'll join you.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.950
What's that?

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.460
I got a bug bite.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.320
It's not a hickey, is it?

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:27.330
Of course not!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.660
Let me see it.

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.740
Grandma, you come
and swim with us.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.070
Grandma, you're a good swimmer.

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:41.370
In the old days, they called me
the Queen of the Beach.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.500
C'mon, Yusaku!
I'll race you!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.370
Stop it, Grandma.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.750
She's pretty fast.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.450
Dried squid came from
the sea, after all.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.990
Don't say that
about your grandmother!

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:56.960
Don't you think she
looks like dried squid?

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.370
This feels great.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.570
Sure does.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.340
Your bandage.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.440
Oops! Where did it go?

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:21.210
It didn't look
like a bug bite,

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:23.950
but it couldn't be...

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.120
Don't scare me
like that, Grandma!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:33.620
Oh?

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:43.200
Good for you! You've
finally become a man!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.000
What're you saying, Grandma?

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.760
Don't try to deny it.
I know what that is.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.770
It's a hickey!

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.470
N-No, it's not.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:54.800
I thought you'd been
coming home late lately.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:55.900
Now it makes sense.

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:57.250
Who gave it to you?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.550
Was it Kozue, or
that high school girl?

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:01.910
Please! This is-

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.540
Come to think of it

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.220
you never came home
the night before last.

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.960
I called you and told you

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.150
that I'd stay over
at Sakamoto's!

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.520
I-It's true!
In fact, Sakamoto-

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.870
Hello, Manager!

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:19.890
Sakamoto?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.400
I work here part-time!

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.070
Godai, you're here too?

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:25.840
Sakamoto, what do you
think you're doing?

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.080
What are you doing
during your break?

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.110
Can't you SEE what I'm doing?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:35.910
Regardless, Godai, I'm still
hurting over a bad breakup.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.620
Are you going to make
me hurt even more?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.730
What about me?

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.420
Let's keep it to ourselves.
We'd both be embarrassed.

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:49.970
Waiter, bring us
sekihan black-bean rice.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.300
We're celebrating a boy's
transition into manhood.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.130
I'm sorry, but we
don't serve sekihan here.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.610
Oh? Where's the manager?

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.160
She got out.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:07.870
I don't care if it
was Kozue or whomever.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.490
But I wonder who it was?

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.760
This is on me.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:20.470
Thank you.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:23.150
It's my pleasure, Manager.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.170
Sakamoto!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.290
What's that get up?

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.390
I'm a waiter here.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:33.170
Great! More beer please!

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.750
Keep it flowing!

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:38.620
Yes. Well, I have to go.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.040
I heard Godai stayed with
you two nights ago?

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:49.360
Godai? I don't think so.
No one came two nights ago.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:50.860
Did he say he did?

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.920
N-No.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.570
I knew it was a lie.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:02.030
Manager, it's all
a misunderstanding.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.710
I got this when Sakamoto-

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.480
It's a hickey!

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.740
I'm impressed, Godai!

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.840
Who put it there?

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.980
I'm trying to tell
you that Sakamoto-

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:18.660
Sakamoto said no one stayed
with him two nights ago.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.690
He's embarrassed.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:23.230
It's nothing to
be embarrassed about.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:28.160
I get those all the time.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:30.760
It's nothing to brag about.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.200
If a girl gave it to me,
I'd brag about it.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:41.270
It's not something
to brag about, really.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:45.860
Manager!

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:03.130
It's a misunderstanding!

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:04.860
Let it go.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.030
I can't!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.710
Now they're racing.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:22.650
Manager?!

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:24.180
Ms. Otonashi?!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:31.060
Leg cramp!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.330
Oh gosh! I'm holding her!

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:47.750
He beat me to her!

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.480
A-Are you all right?

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:50.880
Yes.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:01.320
I hate you!

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:06.700
What's happening?

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:10.680
She shouldn't get so mad
about a hickey or two.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:13.640
They're both so easily provoked.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.070
What's up between
Yusaku and the manager?

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:22.170
You're asking a
very scary question.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.840
I've been meaning to
figure it out myself.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.550
EMPLOYEE LOUNGE
A hickey and a bite mark?
Way to go!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:30.890
A hickey and a bite mark?
Way to go!

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.960
S-She's very intense.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:35.780
You're something else!

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:39.360
Actually, I gave
him that hickey.

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:41.730
You mean you two are--?!

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:42.970
Right, Godai?

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.140
This is all your fault.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:19:59.540
I'm sorry.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:11.730
My top!

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:15.030
Ms. Otonashi, why
don't you come out now?

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.060
Please stay away!

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.700
Have I said something
to offend you?

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:19.860
N-No!

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:22.100
I just want to be
alone for a while.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:23.520
I see.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.100
What's wrong, Ms. Otonashi?

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:29.880
You're not your
usual self today.

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:37.510
I wanted Mrs. Ichinose or
Akemi to get me a towel,

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.630
but look at them!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.400
What'll I do?

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.900
I wonder if the manager's
still swimming?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.860
Please don't run!

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.270
I'll be okay!

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.250
What'll I do?

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:03.660
My--!

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:14.890
Waiter?!

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:31.070
That waiter looked a lot like Godai
but he couldn't have been-

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:42.150
Sake after a good swim
hits the spot!

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:44.390
Did you swim, Mrs. Ichinose?

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:51.520
About Godai's hickey-

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:53.900
I'm not interested.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.520
You're not interested
in the truth behind it?

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:08.950
Sakamoto gave him
that hickey? Really?

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:16.690
I'm back!

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:20.850
Welcome home. How did it go?

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:21.500
Huh?

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:25.000
You said you had
an interview this afternoon.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:28.020
I don't think it went too well.

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:31.830
I see. You'll have other opportunities.

00:22:31.980 --> 00:22:33.000
Y-Yes.

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:37.300
Next spring, I'll
be a working man.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:39.570
I'll do my best.

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:44.610
See you.

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:49.980
Thank you for
saving me at the pool.

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:51.350
You're welcome.

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:04.360
A summer job as a waiter
is nothing to be ashamed about.

00:23:04.600 --> 00:23:05.730
I'm sorry.

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:23.590
What's this?

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.930
A Fine summer day
My arms are stinging sweetly
As cicadas sing

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.400
by Yusaku.

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:35.790
What's this?

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:48.070
Hey! It's stopped!

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:49.770
There was an accident
on the train line.

00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:54.100
Then let's drink up 'til the
train starts running again!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:00.100
Next time:
"Farewell Grandma!
Party on Down at Ueno Station"

00:24:00.180 --> 00:24:02.980
Yusaku! Where do you
think you're going?
